<p>North Korea opened its Workers’ Party congress on February 20, a meeting held every five years where leader Kim Jong Un is expected to lay out domestic and foreign policy priorities for the next cycle. In his opening address, Kim pointed to efforts to boost economic activity and said the economy is gaining strength — a signal that living standards and production targets will sit near the top of the agenda.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/zjtaI5LB9WEKsS7dMUcC81mEplwASLEn_CLidXRDYFB5maoA8mUSA6uaLWmkbTeBlB1IPMrcpPmC6jyvkBInM26l44JzShrH9t3w8i6Lf_LJo3Fo2rmba2HQ0xnGsj4kTRlcheD03LMPNK7ghaZBHNxTLmEgEPgQfVFVITikAA4sVr1WeGkIRNaOO-Ck62D2O-fnu1fv' alt='Kim Jong Un speaks as North Korea opens its Workers’ Party congress.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>State-planning scope: The congress is more than a venue for broad slogans. It often serves as a place to steer practical state planning, from construction drives to security and military planning.</li><li>Ninth Congress framing: Al Jazeera described the gathering as the Ninth Congress of the Workers’ Party of Korea, with Kim using the opening session to spotlight stronger economic activity.</li><li>Power consolidation: Coverage also flagged expectations that the meeting will reinforce the Kim family’s authoritarian rule, as the party reaffirms leadership lines and national objectives.</li><li>Analyst assessment: Analysts quoted by the Financial Times said the government appears to be in its strongest geopolitical and economic position in years, shaping expectations for a confident policy posture.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Kim Jong Un: In his opening address, Kim stressed boosting economic activity and portrayed the economy as rising, pointing to a coming focus on production and livelihoods. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/20/north-koreas-kim-jong-un-launches-key-party-congress-held-every-5-years'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Deutsche Welle: DW described the congress as the leadership’s main forum for setting policy direction and priorities for the next stretch. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-opens-key-party-congress/a-76052057'>Deutsche Welle</a>)</li><li>ABC News: ABC News highlighted expectations that the congress will further entrench the Kim family’s authoritarian rule, as party elites line up behind official leadership and goals. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/north-korea-opens-major-party-congress-kim-emphasizing-130320902'>ABC News</a>)</li><li>Financial Times: The FT pointed to analysts who say Pyongyang has strengthened its geopolitical and economic position, which could shape the tone and ambition of the congress’s decisions. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/620a5268-a147-464f-8bf9-1b967efcb210'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>The Hindu: The Hindu emphasized the gathering’s broad remit, framing it as a meeting that sets direction for everything from housing drives to military planning. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/kim-jong-un-opens-rare-party-congress-in-north-korea/article70654564.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-opens-key-party-congress/a-76052057'>North Korea&#x27;s Kim Jong Un opens key party congress</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/20/north-koreas-kim-jong-un-launches-key-party-congress-held-every-5-years'>North Korea’s Kim Jong Un launches key party congress held every 5 years</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/north-korea-opens-major-party-congress-kim-emphasizing-130320902'>North Korea opens major party congress with Kim emphasizing economy</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/620a5268-a147-464f-8bf9-1b967efcb210'>North Korea’s Kim Jong Un triumphant at rare congress</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/kim-jong-un-opens-rare-party-congress-in-north-korea/article70654564.ece'>Kim Jong Un opens rare party congress in North Korea</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>